/// registry listing carries PROVIDERS; a discovery queue carries RESOURCES; a
/// single job (one resource to fetch, small enough to travel as the context of
/// one HTTP request) carries one RESOURCES entry; a storage receipt carries
/// RECEIPTS; a retriever reports STATUS and is configured with SETTINGS.
///
/// Neighbouring standards: a provider configured as a running ingest source on
/// a node is an $ICN (ingest connector), which SRG nests rather than repeats.
/// SRG describes where data comes from; $DAV says whether a node holds the
/// latest published dataset of a lane, and $PNM announces a publication.
/// Neither fits a storage receipt: a $PNM is a signed network announcement and
/// a $DAV describes a whole lane, while a receipt only states that given bytes
/// were stored under a content identifier. A receipt's CID is what a later
/// $NCD (SOURCE_CID), $DPM asset or $PNM refers to. Coverage reuses the
